From 6993fa0f023eeabe13b0fc3abe7996b272e1deba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UZDoom NX2 <uzdoom-nx2@users.noreply.local>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:42:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 72/72] Switch 2 0.1.3: no BSP worker deadlock, gyro and rumble
 in the game's menus

- The freezes on the first frame of a level (Freedoom: Phase 1, Brutal
  Doom, BENCH 2/3) were the game thread waiting in RenderBSP for the
  gl_multithread worker, which never ran (hang.log). gl_multithread is off
  by default on the Switch 2; when turned on, the worker no longer has a
  fixed core and its empty-queue loop yields.
- hang.log also dumps the render worker and the process core mask.
- Gyro aiming in Controller Options (IfOption(Switch2), LANGUAGE strings in
  English, French and Portuguese): on/off (off by default), horizontal and
  vertical sensitivity (3.5 / 1.5), inversion, level-the-view command; the
  reset is bindable in Customize Controls > Actions.
- Gyro rotation integrated sample by sample (smoother).
- Rumble (haptics_strength) off by default on the Switch 2; the watchdog
  stops it when frames stop (a frozen game no longer keeps vibrating).
- Configs migrated once (rd_defaults_rev 5).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
